      {
        "id": "act_animated_2jac",
        "name": "Animated",
        "actionType": "trait",
        "descriptionHtml": "<p>If the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0.</p><p>When the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.</p><p>The DM might rule that a specific objects slam attack inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form.</p>",
        "macro": {
